{'review': '{\n  "review": {\n    "overall_status": "NEEDS_FIXES",\n    "quality_score": 6.5,\n    "summary": {\n      "critical": 0,\n      "high": 0,\n      "medium": 3,\n      "low": 2,\n      "passed_checks": [\n        "Type annotations",\n        "No hardcoded secrets",\n        "Stable state setters",\n        "Effect dependency correct",\n        "Centralized error state"\n      ]\n    },\n    "findings": [\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-001",\n        "severity": "low",\n        "category": "performance",\n        "title": "Sorted todos computed on every render without memoization",\n        "file": "src/hooks/useTodos.ts",\n        "line_range": [86, 94],\n        "description": "The sortedTodos variable is calculated during each render, causing unnecessary computation if the todos list is large or the component renders frequently.",\n        "impact": "Performance degradation, especially with large todo lists or frequent re-renders.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Wrap the sortedTodos calculation in useMemo with dependencies todos, sortBy, sortOrder.",\n        "code_before": "const sortedTodos = [...todos].sort((a, b) => {\\n    let compare = 0;\\n    if (sortBy === \'title\') {\\n      compare = a.title.localeCompare(b.title);\\n    } else if (sortBy === \'completed\') {\\n      compare = (a.completed === b.completed) ? 0 : a.completed ? 1 : -1;\\n    }\\n    return sortOrder === \'asc\' ? compare : -compare;\\n  });",\n        "code_after": "const sortedTodos = useMemo(() => {\\n    return [...todos].sort((a, b) => {\\n      let compare = 0;\\n      if (sortBy === \'title\') {\\n        compare = a.title.localeCompare(b.title);\\n      } else if (sortBy === \'completed\') {\\n        compare = (a.completed === b.completed) ? 0 : a.completed ? 1 : -1;\\n      }\\n      return sortOrder === \'asc\' ? compare : -compare;\\n    });\\n  }, [todos, sortBy, sortOrder]);",\n        "references": []\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-002",\n        "severity": "medium",\n        "category": "quality",\n        "title": "Unsafe access to err.message without verifying err is an Error instance",\n        "file": "src/hooks/useTodos.ts",\n        "line_range": [30, 30],\n        "description": "The catch block assumes err has a message property, but err could be null, undefined, or a non-object value, leading to a runtime error when accessing err.message.",\n        "impact": "If the thrown value is not an Error object, accessing err.message will throw TypeError, breaking error handling and potentially causing the UI to crash.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Check if err is an Error instance before accessing its message, or use a fallback string.",\n        "code_before": "    } catch (err: any) {\\n      setError(err.message);\\n    } finally {",\n        "code_after": "    } catch (err: any) {\\n      const message = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);\\n      setError(message);\\n    } finally {",\n        "references": [\n          "https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/everyday-types.html#type-guards-and-assertions"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-003",\n        "severity": "medium",\n        "category": "quality",\n        "title": "Potential race condition/stale data in fetchTodos due to missing request cancellation",\n        "file": "src/hooks/useTodos.ts",\n        "line_range": [17, 34],\n        "description": "When the filter changes rapidly, multiple fetchTodos requests may be in flight. If an older request resolves after a newer one, it can overwrite the todos state with stale data.",\n        "impact": "UI may display outdated todo list, causing confusion and inconsistency.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Use an AbortController to cancel previous requests, or track a request ID and ignore stale responses.",\n        "code_before": "  const fetchTodos = useCallback(async () => {\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    try {\\n      let completedFilter: boolean | undefined;\\n      if (filter === \'active\') {\\n        completedFilter = false;\\n      } else if (filter === \'completed\') {\\n        completedFilter = true;\\n      }\\n      const data = await getTodos(completedFilter);\\n      setTodos(data);\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      setError(err.message);\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  }, [filter]);",\n        "code_after": "  const fetchTodos = useCallback(async () => {\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    const abortController = new AbortController();\\n    try {\\n      let completedFilter: boolean | undefined;\\n      if (filter === \'active\') {\\n        completedFilter = false;\\n      } else if (filter === \'completed\') {\\n        completedFilter = true;\\n      }\\n      const data = await getTodos(completedFilter, { signal: abortController.signal });\\n      setTodos(data);\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      if (err.name !== \'AbortError\') {\\n        setError(err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err));\\n      }\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoading(false);\\n    }\\n    return () => abortController.abort();\\n  }, [filter]);",\n        "references": []\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-004",\n        "severity": "low",\n        "category": "quality",\n        "title": "Loading state may be incorrectly set due to overlapping getTodo calls",\n        "file": "src/hooks/useTodos.ts",\n        "line_range": [72, 84],\n        "description": "The getTodo function sets loading state to true on each call without tracking concurrent requests. If multiple getTodo calls overlap, loading may be set to false prematurely when the first request finishes, while other requests are still pending.",\n        "impact": "UI may show loading spinner incorrectly, leading to poor user experience.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Use a loading counter or separate loading state per request, or cancel previous requests.",\n        "code_before": "  const getTodo = useCallback(async (id: string) => {\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    try {\\n      const todo = await getTodoById(id);\\n      return todo;\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      setError(err.message);\\n      throw err;\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  }, []);",\n        "code_after": "  const getTodo = useCallback(async (id: string) => {\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    try {\\n      const todo = await getTodoById(id);\\n      return todo;\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      const message = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);\\n      setError(message);\\n      throw err;\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  }, []);",\n        "references": []\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-005",\n        "severity": "low",\n        "category": "quality",\n        "title": "Unnecessary rethrow after setting error state may cause unhandled promise rejection",\n        "file": "src/hooks/useTodos.ts",\n        "line_range": [40, 49],\n        "description": "After setting the error state, the functions rethrow the caught error. If the caller does not handle the rejected promise, it results in an unhandled promise rejection warning.",\n        "impact": "Potential unhandled promise rejection warnings in the console, and possible crashes if not caught.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Remove the throw err; line after setting error state, unless the caller explicitly needs to handle the error.",\n        "code_before": "  const addTodo = useCallback(async (payload: CreateTodoPayload) => {\\n    try {\\n      const newTodo = await createTodo(payload);\\n      setTodos((prev) => [...prev, newTodo]);\\n      return newTodo;\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      setError(err.message);\\n      throw err;\\n    }\\n  }, []);",\n        "code_after": "  const addTodo = useCallback(async (payload: CreateTodoPayload) => {\\n    try {\\n      const newTodo = await createTodo(payload);\\n      setTodos((prev) => [...prev, newTodo]);\\n      return newTodo;\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      setError(err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err));\\n    }\\n  }, []);",\n        "references": []\n      }\n    ],\n    "positive_observations": [\n      "Proper use of TypeScript with explicit types for state and props.",\n      "Effective use of useCallback to prevent unnecessary re-creations.",\n      "Correct dependency arrays for useEffect and useCallback.",\n      "Centralized error state management.",\n      "Clear separation of concerns for CRUD operations.",\n      "No hardcoded secrets or sensitive data."\n    ]\n  }\n}'}